# the nudge: a layer's button held (ENV the chord, ARP the pings, LFO the bass, SEQ the drums) moves its sound a
# step (a walk pulled back to the piece's recipe), says the biggest change and shows the layer's sound page; held
# on, a shake (a new voice or kit, every value a big step);
# a tap is the page, as ever. Evolve nudges by itself, now and then on a phrase's first bar: at 100 it does, at 40
# (and under) never
listen
wait 2000
press ENV
wait 700
release ENV
wait 300
said CHORD NUDGE
expect view 8
press ARP
wait 700
release ARP
wait 300
said PINGS NUDGE
expect view 9
press LFO
wait 700
release LFO
wait 300
said BASS NUDGE
expect view 10
press SEQ
wait 700
release SEQ
wait 300
said DRUMS NUDGE
expect view 11
# held on (1.5 s): a shake, a new voice (Basic's chord: Saws, 0) and every value a big step
press ENV
wait 1800
release ENV
wait 300
said CHORD SHAKE
expect par22 >0
expect view 8
# held on, the drums: another kit
press SEQ
wait 1800
release SEQ
wait 300
said DRUMS SHAKE
expect par35 >0
# the bass held on: a shake, a new voice and a new groove (a neighbour)
press LFO
wait 1800
release LFO
wait 300
said BASS SHAKE
expect view 10
# FX, the space: a nudge, then held on a shake (a new echo time); the Space page
press FX
wait 700
release FX
wait 300
said SPACE NUDGE
expect view 5
press FX
wait 1800
release FX
wait 300
said SPACE SHAKE
# a tap: the page (no nudge)
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
said_none NUDGE
# Evolve 40: two minutes playing, nothing nudged (saved, then still saved)
tap HOME
wait 300
expect view 0
spin K2 -15
wait 200
expect par5 40
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
wait 300
expect dirty 0
wait 120000
expect dirty 0
# Evolve 100: two minutes, the sound nudged (the project changed)
spin K2 60
wait 200
expect par5 100
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
wait 300
expect dirty 0
wait 120000
expect dirty 1
# a nudge of yours shows a card in the middle (amber), a shake's red; Evolve's don't; gone after ~1.8 s
tap HOME
wait 2500
expect card 0
press ENV
wait 700
release ENV
wait 200
expect card 1
wait 2000
expect card 0
press LFO
wait 1700
release LFO
wait 200
expect card 2
# every long press its card: EDIT held (the next chord), held on (new chords, red); GLO held (saved), held on (reset)
wait 2000
press EDIT
wait 700
release EDIT
wait 200
expect card 1
wait 2000
press EDIT
wait 1700
release EDIT
wait 200
expect card 2
wait 2000
press GLO
wait 700
release GLO
wait 200
expect card 1
wait 2000
press GLO
wait 1700
release GLO
wait 200
expect card 2
# HOME held on: a shake of everything (the chord's, the pings', the bass's voices and the kit, the noise's character);
# the page kept; HOME with SELECT turned is still the tempo
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
turn PRESET 1
turn PRESET -1
press GLO
wait 1700
release GLO
wait 300
expect par22 0
expect par35 0
press HOME
wait 1700
release HOME
wait 200
said SHAKE EVERYTHING
expect card 2
expect view 1
expect par22 !=0
expect par35 !=0
